/-
# Fixed subgroups of automorphisms of free pro-`p` groups (Kourovka Notebook Problem 12.70)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 12.70 (L. Ribes): let `F` be a free pro-`p`
group of finite rank and `Δ ≠ 1` an automorphism of `F` whose order is a power of `p`. Is the rank
of `Fix_F(Δ) = {x ∈ F | Δ(x) = x}` finite?
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.PGroup
public import Mathlib.Topology.Algebra.Group.Subgroup

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.FreeProPFixedSubgroupKourovka12Problem70Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 12.70 (L.
Ribes). UnsolvedMath record UM-00700888 (`KOU-12.70`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

Pro-`p` groups are compact Hausdorff totally disconnected groups whose open normal subgroups have
`p`-power index. A free pro-`p` group of rank `d` is a pro-`p` group topologically generated by `x₀,
…, x_{d-1}` such that every assignment of the `xᵢ` in a finite `p`-group extends to a continuous
homomorphism (one with open kernel); this characterizes the free pro-`p` group on the `xᵢ`. `Δ` is
assumed continuous (automatic for finitely generated pro-`p` groups by Serre's theorem). Finite rank
of `Fix_F(Δ)` means that it is the closure of the subgroup generated by finitely many of its
elements.
-/

/-- A pro-`p` group: a compact Hausdorff totally disconnected group whose open normal subgroups
have `p`-power index. -/
def IsProP (p : ℕ) (G : Type) [Group G] [TopologicalSpace G] : Prop :=
  CompactSpace G ∧ T2Space G ∧ TotallyDisconnectedSpace G ∧
    ∀ N : Subgroup G, N.Normal → IsOpen (N : Set G) → ∃ k : ℕ, N.index = p ^ k

/-- `F` is a free pro-`p` group on `x₀, …, x_{d-1}`: a pro-`p` group topologically generated by
the `xᵢ` such that every assignment of the `xᵢ` in a finite `p`-group `P` extends to a continuous
homomorphism `F → P` (one with open kernel). -/
def IsFreeProPOn (p d : ℕ) (F : Type) [Group F] [TopologicalSpace F] [IsTopologicalGroup F]
    (x : Fin d → F) : Prop :=
  IsProP p F ∧ (Subgroup.closure (Set.range x)).topologicalClosure = ⊤ ∧
    ∀ (P : Type) [Group P] [Finite P], IsPGroup p P → ∀ y : Fin d → P,
      ∃ φ : F →* P, IsOpen (φ.ker : Set F) ∧ ∀ i, φ (x i) = y i

/-- Kourovka 12.70 (L. Ribes): if `F` is a free pro-`p` group of finite rank and `Δ ≠ 1` is a
(continuous) automorphism of `F` of `p`-power order, then `Fix_F(Δ)` has finite rank, i.e. it is
the closure of the subgroup generated by finitely many of its elements. -/
def fixedSubgroupFinitelyGenerated : Prop :=
  ∀ p : ℕ, p.Prime → ∀ (d : ℕ) (F : Type) [Group F] [TopologicalSpace F] [IsTopologicalGroup F]
    (x : Fin d → F), IsFreeProPOn p d F x →
    ∀ Δ : MulAut F, Continuous Δ → Δ ≠ 1 → (∃ k : ℕ, Δ ^ (p ^ k) = 1) →
      ∃ S : Finset F, (∀ s ∈ S, Δ s = s) ∧
        ((Subgroup.closure (S : Set F)).topologicalClosure : Set F) = {z | Δ z = z}

/--
Resolved true: the Kourovka Archive answers 12.70 "Yes, it is finite" (C. Scheiderer, 1999);
moreover, the fixed points of a finite `p`-group of automorphisms of a free pro-`p` group form a
free factor (Herfort, Ribes and Zalesskii, 1999), which has finite rank when `F` does. Source: E. I.
Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st
issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 12.70 (L. Ribes); resolution:
C. Scheiderer, Proc. Amer. Math. Soc. 127 (1999), no. 3, 695-700; W. N. Herfort, L. Ribes and P. A.
Zalesskii, Forum Math. 11 (1999), no. 1, 49-61, Kourovka Archive, Problem 12.70: Yes, it is finite
(Scheiderer); the fixed points of a finite p-group of automorphisms form a free factor
(Herfort-Ribes-Zalesskii).
-/
public theorem_wanted fixedSubgroupFinitelyGenerated_holds : fixedSubgroupFinitelyGenerated

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.FreeProPFixedSubgroupKourovka12Problem70Wanted
